+/* Windows Animation: variables whose values follow transitions scheduled on
+ * storyboards, advanced by the manager's Update (usually driven by the
+ * animation timer). Transitions are functions of time from a variable's
+ * value and velocity when they start; a storyboard lays them out in time
+ * (one after another per variable, or at keyframes); the manager evaluates
+ * every playing storyboard at the time it is updated to and tells the
+ * handlers what changed. */
